  "clean_text": "The Joy of Learning | Sankara The Joy of Learning | Sankara About Services Social Impact Donate Pledge Your Eyes Education Careers Our Blog Contact Services About Us About Pledge Your Eyes Contact Education Social Impact Services Donate Awards Dr.RVR Awards and Biography lasikblr Sankara Lasik Services OUR STORY SERVICES SOCIAL IMPACT The Joy of Learning Students | 4 MIN READ January 25, 2018 The Joy of Learning A SAV CASE STUDY THE JOY OF LEARNING DR AZHARUDDIN (PDDNB 2013 JAN, SHIMOGA, DNB RESIDENT) Now that I am a Consultant Phacosurgeon in one of reputed Eye Hospital in Kerala, I felt the need to thank the institute to which I belong. After the blessings of Almighty, the one thing which happened to me which played a very important role in making me what I am today is Sankara Eye Hospital-Shimoga. Also, the prophet of Islam (Pbuh) is reported to have said “He who doesn’t thank people, doesn’t thank God.”\u0003 The journey of 2 years had been a wonderful experience, the joy of learning directly from the stalwarts of Ophthalmology like Dr SB Sir, Dr Sathyan sir, Dr MPS sir in the form of regular Video Conferencing or practical surgical tips being right besides with the Specialists like Dr SM sir, Dr KV ma’am is beyond what words can describe.\u0003 A comparatively rare thing in teaching institutes, which I noticed throughout my residency was the ease of approachability and this I say without exaggeration! I was free to come and discuss any doubt I had, even while the surgeon is operating, they made sure they clear the doubt at the very same moment. \u0003 Though there are innumerable such experiences, I would like to share only two of those which I can never forget in my life. Both the instances during my infancy in Sankara. The first one was with Dr KV mam, the first month of my OT Postings, I was tense and happened to come to observe her surgery. She very calmly enquired about my surgery and difficulties, about my technique and advised me to operate during my beginning few case..."
